  ("Open with a neutral suspended chord, sus2 (1-2-5) or sus4 (1-4-5), over a low root note, then move to the minor triad.","Pad synth","A suspended, ethereal start resolving to the key's colour."),
  ("Add contrast with a 7sus-style shape (root, 5th, 7th) and return to the suspended or minor chords; stick to 2-4 notes per chord.","Pad synth","Variation without leaving the key."),
  ("Make variants from the same notes: inversions (different chord tone in the bass), dropping tones down 1-2 octaves, or using a non-root chord tone as the next chord's root.","Piano roll","The same chord sounds new."),
